# Everything the image must not carry.
#
# The first entry is the one that matters: .env holds a live MongoDB
# URI, a billable Azure key and the JWT signing secret. A COPY that
# picks it up writes those into a layer, and a layer keeps them even if
# a later step deletes the file - including in any registry the image
# reaches. Configuration is passed as environment variables instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Machine-specific and large. .venv in particular is built for the host
# OS and would break the image even if it fitted.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Needs a live sandbox connection; no business in a runtime image.
app/tests/

# Dev-only by the project's own definition, and two of them WRITE.
# See the Dockerfile's header for why a read-only service does not
# ship them.
scripts/

# Reference material, some of it holding real captured production data
# (see .gitignore). None of it is read at run time.
docs/

.git/
.github/
.claude/
*.log
test_output.txt
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
